// Microsoft OAuth client for "Sign in with Microsoft" (backlog item 31, T31-2;
// docs/architecture/sign-in-first.md 4.2 and 4.7).
//
// Committed with an EMPTY value: a build made from the repo as-is (CI, forks,
// contributors) has Microsoft sign-in switched off and the provider reports
// "not configured". To switch it on for a build, supply the Sentwise-owned
// Entra application (client) ID either:
//
//   1. locally: copy MicrosoftOAuth.local.xcconfig.example to
//      MicrosoftOAuth.local.xcconfig (git-ignored) and fill it in, or
//   2. in CI/release: pass `SENTWISE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=...` on the xcodebuild
//      command line (Distribution/scripts/release.sh does this from the
//      repository secret of the same name; command-line settings win).
//
// Info.plist expands it into SentwiseMicrosoftOAuthClientID, read by
// MicrosoftOAuthClientConfiguration. The app is a public client: there is NO
// client secret setting and none is ever sent (Microsoft answers a secret
// from a public client with AADSTS700025). Authority is `common`, the redirect
// is http://localhost:<port>, and the scopes live in code
// (OAuthProviderConfiguration.microsoft). The ID is not secret, but a real one
// is never committed here.
//
// This file is pulled in through GoogleOAuth.xcconfig, which is the base
// configuration of the Debug and Release build configurations.

SENTWISE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID =

#include? "MicrosoftOAuth.local.xcconfig"
